## S5 setup: drop the copy's remote-tracking ref for the task branch, so its commit is held only by the forge's MR head ref (the precondition the GitLab proof guards: no remote-tracking ref proves the work landed)
$ git -C $LAB/projects/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture update-ref -d refs/remotes/origin/fm/nm-7226-live
[exit 0]
$ git -C $LAB/wt log --oneline HEAD --not --remotes   # commits on no remote-tracking ref
7d1d801 fixture: gate live validation first commit (throwaway)
[exit 0]
$ git -C $LAB/wt merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD refs/fm-review/mr/3/head && echo 'HEAD is contained in the MR head ref'
HEAD is contained in the MR head ref
[exit 0]
$ glab mr view 3 -R gh0stwin/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture -F json | jq -r .state
opened
[exit 0]
## S5 (adversarial): teardown refuses while the merge request is open, though its head ref holds the work
$ fm-teardown.sh nm-7226-live
fm-gate-refuse: gate agent lifecycle permitted only against lab home $LAB
REFUSED: worktree $LAB/wt has work not on any remote and not landed.
unpushed commits:
7d1d801 fixture: gate live validation first commit (throwaway)
Push the branch, land its PR, or get the captain's explicit OK to discard, then --force.
[exit 1]
## state retained after the refusal
$ test -d $LAB/wt && git -C $LAB/wt rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD && git -C $LAB/wt rev-parse HEAD
fm/nm-7226-live
7d1d801262fc56fefa967d1ce931cf30a9f6904b
[exit 0]
